WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.638
Writing files safely requires planning for partial failure.

2
00:00:02.638 --> 00:00:09.894
A write may fail because permissions changed, storage filled, a process was interrupted, the destination moved, encoding failed, or the system shut

3
00:00:09.894 --> 00:00:10.553
down unexpectedly.

4
00:00:10.553 --> 00:00:17.149
If the program assumes that a write either fully succeeds or never changes anything, it may leave corrupted state behind.

5
00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:18.469
Truncation should be intentional.

6
00:00:18.469 --> 00:00:26.384
Opening an existing file in a mode that clears it before new data is safely available can turn a recoverable failure into data loss.

7
00:00:26.384 --> 00:00:34.958
For many update workflows, a temporary-write-then-replace pattern is safer at a high level: write the new contents to a separate file, check the

8
00:00:34.958 --> 00:00:40.565
result, and then replace the old file using the most appropriate operation for the platform and filesystem.

9
00:00:40.565 --> 00:00:45.182
The exact durability and atomicity details vary, so document what the application relies on.

10
00:00:45.182 --> 00:00:48.810
Sensitive output needs careful permissions from the moment it is created.

11
00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:53.427
It is weaker to create broadly readable data and try to restrict it later.

12
00:00:53.427 --> 00:00:57.384
Output paths should still pass the same path policy as input paths.

13
00:00:57.384 --> 00:01:03.651
A program should also avoid mixing trusted generated output with caller-controlled filenames unless the policy clearly allows it.

14
00:01:03.651 --> 00:01:06.289
Correctness may depend on errors that appear late.

15
00:01:06.289 --> 00:01:07.938
Stream writes can buffer data.

16
00:01:07.938 --> 00:01:12.885
Flush and close operations can reveal failures after the main write call appeared to succeed.

17
00:01:12.885 --> 00:01:20.470
When durable output matters, check the relevant outcomes, report failure safely, and leave the application in a state that can be retried or

18
00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:20.800
recovered.
